title: Implement cooperative preemption and yield injection
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-04T05:31:38'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T14:43:57'
result: 'Implemented cooperative preemption via compiler-inserted yields. NEW MIR
  pass src/mir/opt/yield_passes.rs::inject_yields: detects loop back-edges (reachability:
  edge src->dst where dst reaches src) and inserts a __sched_yield call at each back-edge
  source block, but ONLY in coroutine/actor functions (is_coroutine || name starts_with
  __actor_). Runs at every opt level (correctness pass, wired before the OptLevel::None
  early-return in opt/mod.rs). Opt-out: @no_yield function attribute (added to FnAttrs,
  parsed in parser/decl/fn.rs). codegen magic.rs: __sched_yield -> jinn_sched_yield().
  A tight-loop actor no longer starves siblings — proven by tight_loop_actor_does_not_starve_siblings
  (two actors, one spins 5M iters; both complete, program exits). *main loops correctly
  get no yields (not a coroutine). docs/concurrency.md footgun "must-yield" rewritten
  to document automatic preemption + @no_yield. 11 concurrency tests pass, zero warnings.
  (column_* integration failures are pre-existing on clean tree.)'
description: 'Implement cooperative preemption / yield injection (review 12_safety:
  a handler that never yields starves the scheduler — documented hazard in docs/concurrency.md
  line ~202 ''Every long-running handler must yield''; pthread_join hangs otherwise).
  Current state: grep shows zero preemption machinery in src/ or runtime/. Deliverable:
  compiler-inserted yield points (MIR pass inserting jinn_yield() calls at loop back-edges
  in coroutine/actor contexts — MIR optimization justified because LLVM cannot do
  this) with opt-out attribute, OR runtime timer-driven preemption; pick per design
  discussion. Definition of done: a tight-loop actor no longer starves sibling actors;
  test in tests/concurrency_shutdown.rs with two actors where one spins; docs updated
  to remove the must-yield footgun.'
